    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup is optimized today for high-volume contact and efficiency against a slate of mediocre-to-fair pitching. The strongest play on the board is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), whose elite efficiency score is fueled by a dynamic platoon advantage against Wacha and the stability of the two-hole. Close behind, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.94) remains a must-start despite facing a tougher arm in Tolle; his base projection is simply too high to fade, and he benefits from a strong park factor. **Jackson Merrill** (72.84) also ranks among our elite options, as the matchup against Pallante provides a specific edge for his stolen base potential; his score is propped up by a slow-working pitcher, which historically maximizes our scoring in the scarcest category.\n\nThe most difficult decision for today's roster construction involved leaving **Gunnar Henderson** on the bench. Despite his immense talent, his score of 59.39 was suppressed by a poor matchup against Gilbert, whose elite skill set (low xERA) makes him a dangerous proposition compared to the weaker rotations facing the rest of our starting nine. **Gunnar Henderson** was the primary \"near-miss,\" losing his spot to **Dominic Smith** (59.91) because the latter benefits from a significantly more favorable matchup against Houser, allowing us to capture better projected efficiency for our limited game caps. \n\nWe are keeping a close watch on **Sam Antonacci**, whose 63.14 score is respectable but carries inherent risk due to the presence of Cole on the mound. While we expect him to perform well given his leadoff role, a deep-seated caution remains regarding Cole\u2019s ability to stifle offense regardless of environment. Additionally, managers should monitor the weather in **Cole Carrigg**'s game; while his 56.22 score suggests a marginal start, any shift in wind could impact his fly-ball profile. We are prioritizing high-contact bats today to navigate these matchups, hoping that the aggressive order placements of **Drake Baldwin** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** provide the runs necessary to keep us competitive in a tight 5x5 race.",
